      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Komodo (1999) represents a fascinating entry in the late 90s creature feature boom, arriving in the wake of <a href=\"/movie/9360\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9360\">Anaconda</a> (1997) and <a href=\"/movie/8914\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"8914\">Deep Blue Sea</a> (1999). While lacking the budget of its predecessors, it taps into primal fears of reptilian predators with its story of genetically enhanced Komodo dragons terrorizing a small island. The film follows the low-budget creature feature playbook established by <a href=\"/movie/39283\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"39283\">Carnosaur</a> (1993), using strategic lighting and quick cuts to mask practical effects limitations."
      },
